      "writtenOn": "2022-09-21T14:24:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If doTestPreferBadWifi throws, this code won\u0027t run and the permission will not be dropped. This should go in a finally clause, or better yet use runAsShell:\n\n    // Permanently adopt READ_DEVICE_CONFIG for the duration of the test, because some\n    // classes used by ConnectivityService need to read the device config at multiple points. One such example is MultinetworkPolicyTracker, which reads it on\n    // the handler thread.\n    final boolean preferBadWifi \u003d SdkLevel.isAtLeastU();\n    runAsShell(READ_DEVICE_CONFIG, () -\u003e doTestPreferBadWifi(preferBadWifi));\n\nBut in general it seems better to avoid using the real DeviceConfig class, see above.",
